  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nMuch quieter weather taking hold across the area. Frontal boundary \ncontinues to slide south of the area, with surface high pressure \nbuilding in from the north. Still could be a few showers or storms \ntoday, mainly across the south and east in vicinity of frontal \nboundary and due to heating, along with perhaps a pop up across the \nmountains Thursday afternoon. Otherwise, dry weather will take hold \nuntil Friday into Saturday, when a few weak disturbances will aid in \ngenerating isolated showers and storms, mainly across the south and \neast. Fog can be expected most mornings this week.\n\nFocus then shifts to Sunday into Monday in which upper trough \ndeepens to our east, with amplified NW flow taking hold across the \narea. There are indications of convective complexes forming over the \nmidwest, and moving southeast into our area in this pattern in the \nSunday into Monday time frame. Still a bit too early to tell if \nthere will be much of a severe or flooding threat, but period will \nneed to be monitored as we get closer.",
